{% extends "_layout.html.j2" %}
{% import "_parts.html.j2" as t %}
{% block content %}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px">{% if full_name %}Hi {{ full_name.split(' ')[0] }}.{% else %}Hello,{% endif %}</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 14px">We are doing a one-time migration of the described community collections
out of the legacy Data Commons and into the CKAN catalogue at
<a href="https://dc.cyverse.org">dc.cyverse.org</a>. Of the 103 collections under
<code>/iplant/home/shared</code>, 20 carry full descriptive metadata, and you are named as creator or
contributor on seven of them:</p>

{{ t.counts(collections) }}

<p style="margin:0 0 14px"><b>This is opt-in.</b> If you do not reply, none of these are published.
They stay exactly as they are today: readable in the Data Store, listed in the legacy Data Commons,
absent from the catalogue.</p>

{{ t.unchanged() }}

<p style="margin:0 0 14px"><b>The mapping</b>, fixed for all 20: the collection becomes a CKAN
organization, each folder directly under it becomes a dataset, and the files and folders inside a
dataset become its resources, each linking to its anonymous WebDAV URL. Anything deeper is browsable
over WebDAV but is not a catalogue entry, and a loose file directly under a collection is not
published at all.</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 14px"><b>What arrives.</b> Each organization gets its collection's title,
creator, description, subject, rights and publisher. The dataset level is thinner: across all 20
collections only 7 folders carry a title of their own, so most datasets arrive named after their
directory with an empty description. Filling those in is each organization's own work in CKAN.</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 8px"><b>What I need from you:</b></p>
<ol style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px">
<li style="margin:0 0 8px">Accept or decline, per collection. Partial is fine.</li>
{{ t.admins() }}
{%- set undecided = collections | selectattr('licence_action', 'equalto', 'decide') | list %}
{%- if undecided %}
<li style="margin:0 0 8px">A licence for
{% for c in undecided %}<code>{{ c.collection }}</code>{% if not loop.last %} and {% endif %}{% endfor %},
in a form the catalogue can record: CC-BY-4.0, CC0-1.0, ODC-PDDL-1.0 or similar. Both rights
statements are currently free text that cannot be mapped, so the pages would read
<i>License not specified</i>:
<ul style="margin:6px 0;padding-left:20px">
{%- for c in undecided %}
<li style="margin:0 0 4px"><code>{{ c.collection }}</code> &mdash;
&ldquo;{{ c.licence_current|truncate(150) }}&rdquo;</li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
Tell me the licences and I will write them into the Data Store metadata rather than typing them into
the catalogue, so the values survive.</li>
{%- endif %}
</ol>

<p style="margin:0 0 14px"><b>After the load</b>, six of these hand over: the migration copies the
iRODS metadata once, and from then on the catalogue record is the admins' to edit in CKAN, with
iRODS changes no longer flowing into it. NCEMS is the exception, staying on the hourly sync, so for
NCEMS you keep editing in the Data Store.</p>

{% if staff_asks -%}
<p style="margin:0 0 8px">Two things I need from you as staff, unrelated to your own collections:</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px">
<li style="margin:0 0 8px">Owner lookups on 11 collections I have no contact for, and a twelfth
(<code>terraref</code>) if you cannot say offhand who owns it. The legacy Data Commons
<code>api_stat</code> endpoint exposes no ownership at all, so I need the iRODS ACLs. I have a script
following the <code>irods-adm/user-activity</code> pattern that reads the ACL owners and pipes them
through <code>extract-ldap-user-info</code>; it needs a rodsadmin session and campus network access
to <code>ldap.iplantcollaborative.org</code>, which is why I am asking you rather than running it.</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 8px">Confirmation of who is currently in the <code>cyverse</code>,
<code>esiil</code> and <code>ncems</code> organizations in CKAN. Anonymous callers get an
authorization error on <code>member_list</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p style="margin:0 0 8px">A few metadata cleanups before the first run, since these values become
the organization pages:</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px">
<li style="margin:0 0 6px"><code>NCEMS</code> and <code>genophenoenvo</code> each have a single
<code>Title</code> AVU that reads as a primary title and an alternate title run together with a
comma. NCEMS's is &ldquo;National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular
Sciences (NCEMS), NSF National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences
(NCEMS) Data Repository&rdquo;. Whatever is in that field becomes the organization title verbatim, so
it is worth splitting into a title and an alternate title first.</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px"><code>CHEESEHEAD</code> carries a placeholder AVU literally named
&ldquo;New Attribute&rdquo; with value &ldquo;New Value&rdquo;. It is not one of yours, but it is on
the same run.</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px"><code>geri</code> has 163 metadata fields that should get a read before
they seed an organization description.</li>
</ul>
{%- endif %}

<p style="margin:0 0 14px">The deadline is <b>{{ deadline }}</b>, 60 days out. I will send one
reminder on {{ reminder_date }}. After that the unanswered collections drop out of scope.</p>

{{ t.signature(sender_name, sender_title) }}
{% endblock %}
